<En
  title="Scuba Diving in Shizuoka | Diving Shop ABARO"
  description="PADI dive shop in Shimizu, Shizuoka. English-friendly courses, Izu Peninsula day tours and try-dives. Solo divers welcome, free pick-up from Shimizu, Numazu and Mishima."
  heading="Diving Shop ABARO"
  jaPath="/"
  sub="Shizuoka, Japan"
>
  <p>
    ABARO is a PADI dive centre in Shimizu, Shizuoka, about one hour from Mount Fuji
    and roughly an hour by shinkansen from Tokyo. We run courses and guided tours on
    the Izu Peninsula all year round.
  </p>
  <p>
    We are a small shop, so groups stay small. Solo travellers join almost every tour
    and are genuinely welcome.
  </p>

  <h2>What we offer</h2>
  <h3>Try scuba diving</h3>
  <p>
    A 40-minute dive with an instructor beside you the whole time. No licence and no
    experience needed. Everything is included for <strong>¥12,650</strong>.
  </p>
  <h3>PADI certification courses</h3>
  <p>
    Open Water through Divemaster. Course fees include tuition, sea training, rental
    gear, certification and materials, with no add-ons at the end.
    <a href="/en/courses/">See the courses →</a>
  </p>
  <h3>Guided day tours</h3>
  <p>
    More than thirty dive sites across the Izu Peninsula, plus Chiba, Kanagawa and
    trips further afield. Guiding, facility fees, tanks, insurance and lunch are all
    in the price. <a href="/en/prices/">See tour prices →</a>
  </p>

  <h2>Good to know</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Language</th><td>Our guiding is mainly in Japanese. Staff can handle straightforward English, and we are used to diving with visitors from overseas. Please tell us in advance so we can prepare.</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Getting here</th><td>Shimizu, Shizuoka. Free pick-up from Shimizu, Numazu and Mishima.</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Opening hours</th><td>11:00–20:00, closed Tuesdays.</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Payment</th><td>Cash, major credit cards and electronic money.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Booking</h2>
  <p>
    LINE gets the fastest reply. Phone and email also work.
    <a href="/en/booking/">How to book →</a>
  </p>
</En>
